    "enrich_notes": "Garland TSM references NCTCOG/iSWM and EPA LID resources for sustainable BMP sizing; local checklist defines first-flush detention as (0.08 ft)(C)(A) or storm screening/perforated riser per NCTCOG. Detention design uses 2-, 10-, and 100-year WSEL with first 1-inch rainfall; 1 ft freeboard above 100-year WSEL to emergency spillway crest. Low-flow dewatering device minimum 4-inch diameter; pond access 10 ft minimum unobstructed, max 10% traverse slope (Section 4.11) or 20% on checklist variants.",
